---
config:
  flowchart:
    wrappingWidth: 400
---
flowchart TB
    accTitle: The check of the built website
    accDescr: In every pull request and with every change of main, the check docs builds the website strictly with MkDocs, Material and mkdocs-static-i18n, and after the build the hooks of .github/mkdocs_project.py write security.txt, robots.txt, the pages at the old addresses and the search of every project into the folder site. There blueprint.py site-check checks what the hooks of every website promise, lychee every link and anchor, and scripts/check-site.sh what the hooks of this website promise: security.txt, robots.txt, the sitemaps, the old addresses, the 404 page, the home pages and the search. A broken promise fails the check with the file and the fix, and GitHub Pages publishes only a website that keeps every promise.

    change(["A pull request<br>or a change of main"])
    build["mkdocs build --strict<br>Material · mkdocs-static-i18n"]
    hooks[".github/mkdocs_project.py writes<br>security.txt, robots.txt, the old addresses<br>and the search of every project"]
    site[("site/")]
    blueprint(["blueprint.py site-check<br>the hooks of every website"])
    lychee(["lychee<br>every link and anchor"])
    hub(["scripts/check-site.sh<br>the hooks of this website"])
    fails["The check docs fails<br>with the file and the fix"]
    pages["GitHub Pages<br>dennis-otto.github.io"]

    change --> build --> hooks --> site
    site --> blueprint & lychee & hub
    hub -- "a broken promise" --> fails
    hub -- "every promise kept" --> pages

    classDef bot fill:#526cfe2e,stroke:#526cfe,stroke-width:2px
    classDef warn fill:#dc26262e,stroke:#dc2626,stroke-width:2px
    classDef done fill:#16a34a2e,stroke:#16a34a,stroke-width:2px
    class build,blueprint,lychee,hub bot
    class fails warn
    class pages done
